WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.593 --> 00:00:01.879
- Whatever you're thinking about it,

00:00:01.879 --> 00:00:05.661
you will not get it until you take action.

00:00:05.661 --> 00:00:06.763
Make that move.

00:00:06.763 --> 00:00:10.384
I exist to show people what's possible.

00:00:10.384 --> 00:00:11.562
I really do.

00:00:11.562 --> 00:00:12.984
You need to change.

00:00:12.984 --> 00:00:13.983
Everybody.

00:00:13.983 --> 00:00:15.544
Everybody out there needs to change.

00:00:15.544 --> 00:00:18.836
Life is, you can't predict
what you're supposed to do.

00:00:18.836 --> 00:00:20.276
And I tell people, never kill yourself.

00:00:20.276 --> 00:00:21.558
Never.

00:00:21.558 --> 00:00:23.938
Because you don't know
what your future is.

00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:25.396
- Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:25.396 --> 00:00:26.864
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:26.864 --> 00:00:28.588
My one word is believe and I believe

00:00:28.588 --> 00:00:30.335
that entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:00:30.335 --> 00:00:32.634
all of the major problems of the world,

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:33.970
so to help you on your journey,

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.593
today we're going to learn
from actor Terry Crews

00:00:36.593 --> 00:00:39.763
and my take on his top
ten rules for success.

00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:41.185
Rule number one is my personal favorite

00:00:41.185 --> 00:00:43.727
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:43.727 --> 00:00:45.312
And as always, guys, as you're watching,

00:00:45.312 --> 00:00:47.425
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:47.425 --> 00:00:49.335
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:49.335 --> 00:00:51.524
put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired

00:00:51.524 --> 00:00:54.351
and when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:00:54.351 --> 00:00:56.626
to stick for yourself as well.

00:00:56.626 --> 00:00:57.459
Enjoy.

00:00:58.331 --> 00:01:01.218
(swooshing)

00:01:01.218 --> 00:01:03.718
(grand music)

00:01:11.246 --> 00:01:13.179
- When you're young and you a kid,

00:01:13.179 --> 00:01:15.129
you have so many, I go
up in the hood, man.

00:01:15.129 --> 00:01:16.871
Flint, Michigan, where I'm from

00:01:16.871 --> 00:01:19.329
and they said Terry
Crews, you can do anything

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:20.465
you want to do.

00:01:20.465 --> 00:01:22.037
You can do anything you want to do.

00:01:22.037 --> 00:01:24.574
And then as soon as you go to class,

00:01:24.574 --> 00:01:25.834
you tell them what you want to do

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:27.088
and then they, "Man, what make you think

00:01:27.088 --> 00:01:28.150
"you going to do something like that, man.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.166
"You crazy?"

00:01:29.166 --> 00:01:31.138
And I say, "Okay, wait, which one is it?

00:01:31.138 --> 00:01:32.684
"Now can I do it or can't I do it?"

00:01:32.684 --> 00:01:34.042
- [Interviewer] Right, right.

00:01:34.042 --> 00:01:35.993
- So I started to call people on that.

00:01:35.993 --> 00:01:38.143
I started to call people on that.

00:01:38.143 --> 00:01:40.056
I say, you know what,
I'm going to go for it.

00:01:40.056 --> 00:01:42.860
I'm going to just try something
that I never done before.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.038
I want to design furniture.

00:01:44.038 --> 00:01:45.700
I want to be a part of this thing.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.901
I said I'm going.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:48.224
And you know what happened?

00:01:48.224 --> 00:01:49.425
The stuff worked.

00:01:49.425 --> 00:01:51.699
People started doing,
it started happening.

00:01:51.699 --> 00:01:53.303
(applauding)

00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:55.091
We took the furniture to Milan.

00:01:55.091 --> 00:01:58.487
We went in front of all the best people

00:01:58.487 --> 00:02:00.600
in the whole world and it got accepted

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.074
and people were saying how great it was

00:02:03.074 --> 00:02:04.961
and how beautiful it was and I said, man,

00:02:04.961 --> 00:02:07.038
don't never let anybody
talk you out of something

00:02:07.038 --> 00:02:08.113
like that again.

00:02:08.113 --> 00:02:09.231
- [Interviewer] Never, man.

00:02:09.231 --> 00:02:10.511
- Never.

00:02:10.511 --> 00:02:11.344
- [Interviewer] I'm a dreamer.

00:02:11.344 --> 00:02:12.931
- Take action.

00:02:12.931 --> 00:02:14.539
Whatever you want to do,

00:02:14.539 --> 00:02:15.776
whatever you're thinking about it.

00:02:15.776 --> 00:02:19.470
You will not get it until you take action.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:20.472
Make that move.

00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:21.524
Make it a small step.

00:02:21.524 --> 00:02:24.106
If you want a house, go get a rug.

00:02:24.106 --> 00:02:25.104
You know what I mean?

00:02:25.104 --> 00:02:27.763
If you want a new car, go
get some car freshener.

00:02:27.763 --> 00:02:28.799
Take action.

00:02:28.799 --> 00:02:31.443
Make this thing happen for
you and it will happen.

00:02:31.443 --> 00:02:33.360
Action, action, action.

00:02:34.816 --> 00:02:38.694
You know, one thing that,
you know, I can really

00:02:38.694 --> 00:02:42.630
attribute to every failure in my life,

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:46.797
whether it be personal,
financial, any kind of way,

00:02:49.828 --> 00:02:53.440
business, whatever, it's because of a lack

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.857
of my attempt to take action.

00:02:56.853 --> 00:03:00.985
I did not take action
and it kind of changed,

00:03:00.985 --> 00:03:05.331
once I got the fact
that action is the key,

00:03:05.331 --> 00:03:09.167
it changed my life in many, many ways.

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:11.629
This is where trainers mess people up.

00:03:11.629 --> 00:03:15.629
I've had trainers who
totally just want to prove

00:03:16.589 --> 00:03:20.124
that you could never do what they do.

00:03:20.124 --> 00:03:21.239
And they have you paying.

00:03:21.239 --> 00:03:22.684
- I know what you mean.

00:03:22.684 --> 00:03:24.368
- Just to say like oh, this poor guy.

00:03:24.368 --> 00:03:26.951
And they go to blast
you, like they want you,

00:03:26.951 --> 00:03:28.901
unless you're in pain and you feel

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:30.401
like you're sick and you're throwing up,

00:03:30.401 --> 00:03:31.804
they're like, yeah, that's a workout now.

00:03:31.804 --> 00:03:34.346
Yeah, look at you, you
hurt, you can't walk, great.

00:03:34.346 --> 00:03:37.390
And the whole point is, what I tell people

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:39.950
is treat the gym like a spa.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.961
The first time you ever
go, just go in there

00:03:41.961 --> 00:03:43.504
and walk around, touch the weights,

00:03:43.504 --> 00:03:47.159
get a drink of water, walk
around and then leave.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:50.641
And I mean, literally
do that for like a week,

00:03:50.641 --> 00:03:52.992
two weeks until you just get to the habit

00:03:52.992 --> 00:03:55.961
of getting in that door,
because what's going to happen

00:03:55.961 --> 00:03:57.404
is eventually you're
going to start lifting

00:03:57.404 --> 00:03:58.704
because you're there.

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:00.510
And you're going to do
something and then you stop.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.239
Don't ever get to the
point where you're like

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:03.862
I can't feel my arms!

00:04:03.862 --> 00:04:05.287
It doesn't work.

00:04:05.287 --> 00:04:08.457
People want, they want my
body and all this stuff,

00:04:08.457 --> 00:04:10.222
but I've been working out consistently

00:04:10.222 --> 00:04:12.924
since I was 14 years old and I'm 44.

00:04:12.924 --> 00:04:15.143
- 30 years.
- 30 years.

00:04:15.143 --> 00:04:17.803
- Of hardcore, two hour workouts.

00:04:17.803 --> 00:04:19.167
30 years.

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:20.792
So it doesn't happen overnight.

00:04:20.792 --> 00:04:23.370
You just have to enjoy the process.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.368
Learn to enjoy it because
I'm sure there was a point

00:04:24.368 --> 00:04:28.118
where you started to
enjoy losing 113 pounds.

00:04:30.272 --> 00:04:31.718
- Yep, yep.

00:04:31.718 --> 00:04:32.836
- And that's the only way
you're going to keep going.

00:04:32.836 --> 00:04:35.700
I tell people all the time,
and I really believe this,

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:39.927
is I exist to show people what's possible.

00:04:39.927 --> 00:04:41.203
I really do.

00:04:41.203 --> 00:04:45.799
It's like go for it, try
it because another thing,

00:04:45.799 --> 00:04:48.705
I am no different than
anyone else out there.

00:04:48.705 --> 00:04:50.961
I am not here to say I have a super power

00:04:50.961 --> 00:04:52.703
and it was all this.

00:04:52.703 --> 00:04:56.620
It was just try it, go,
let's see what happens.

00:04:57.543 --> 00:05:00.411
And all of a sudden when
you get rid of judgment,

00:05:00.411 --> 00:05:03.517
now you can be creative, but any bit

00:05:03.517 --> 00:05:06.100
of judgment kills creativity.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.230
Any time you start to go
well, maybe I shouldn't,

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:10.325
and it's funny because
you look at a lip sync

00:05:10.325 --> 00:05:13.533
or you look at any kind of
dancing or anything like that,

00:05:13.533 --> 00:05:15.786
as soon as people see you being inhibited,

00:05:15.786 --> 00:05:18.412
you're done, they're like
oh, this guy, what is this.

00:05:18.412 --> 00:05:23.228
But all they want is for
you to give all you got.

00:05:23.228 --> 00:05:24.444
- [Interviewer] Just put it out there.

00:05:24.444 --> 00:05:26.439
- And then everybody's with you.

00:05:26.439 --> 00:05:27.936
Let me tell you, Terry
Crews is going to give

00:05:27.936 --> 00:05:30.353
you 150% no matter what.

00:05:31.816 --> 00:05:33.892
That's my whole career.

00:05:33.892 --> 00:05:38.118
How many times have you
ever heard the phrase,

00:05:38.118 --> 00:05:40.785
you are perfect just as you are?

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.847
Have you heard that a lot?

00:05:43.847 --> 00:05:44.846
You know what?

00:05:44.846 --> 00:05:46.752
You are perfect just as you are.

00:05:46.752 --> 00:05:48.558
You are so perfect just as you are.

00:05:48.558 --> 00:05:49.577
Well, you know what?

00:05:49.577 --> 00:05:50.616
You are not.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:53.616
You are not perfect just as you are.

00:05:55.777 --> 00:05:59.194
You are perfect, but you're not complete.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.479
This is the thing.

00:06:01.479 --> 00:06:02.604
And this is what I mean by this.

00:06:02.604 --> 00:06:04.754
And a lot of people are going
to go, aw, what do you mean?

00:06:04.754 --> 00:06:05.972
What are you trying to say?

00:06:05.972 --> 00:06:07.008
I got to change?

00:06:07.008 --> 00:06:08.672
I got to change somebody else?

00:06:08.672 --> 00:06:09.671
Yes, yes.

00:06:09.671 --> 00:06:11.723
You need to change.

00:06:11.723 --> 00:06:12.722
Everybody.

00:06:12.722 --> 00:06:15.074
Everybody out there needs to change.

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:16.907
We are designed for change.

00:06:16.907 --> 00:06:18.550
Nothing in this world stays the same.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:20.686
You are either getting better
or you are getting worse.

00:06:20.686 --> 00:06:22.489
Let me describe something to you.

00:06:22.489 --> 00:06:25.684
When I say you are perfect,
but you are not complete,

00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:28.267
let's say this building I'm in.

00:06:29.115 --> 00:06:30.723
If I looked at the
blueprints for this building,

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.985
the blueprints for this building before

00:06:33.985 --> 00:06:36.656
it was built were perfect.

00:06:36.656 --> 00:06:38.158
Everything was in its right place.

00:06:38.158 --> 00:06:40.732
Everything was great,
but could I walk in it?

00:06:40.732 --> 00:06:42.601
Could I do anything?

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:43.622
Did I have a building?

00:06:43.622 --> 00:06:44.637
No.

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:45.636
Why?

00:06:45.636 --> 00:06:46.629
It wasn't complete.

00:06:46.629 --> 00:06:48.579
When they framed up this
building and put wood

00:06:48.579 --> 00:06:51.664
and metal and all this
stuff, but they didn't

00:06:51.664 --> 00:06:54.820
do the floor or the
electrical, was it perfect?

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:58.487
Yes, it was perfect,
but it wasn't complete.

00:07:00.468 --> 00:07:02.699
You are like this building.

00:07:02.699 --> 00:07:05.805
You are perfect in every way,

00:07:05.805 --> 00:07:07.880
but you're just not done.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.425
You're not done and you know what?

00:07:09.425 --> 00:07:11.577
Anybody who's trying
to tell you, don't try

00:07:11.577 --> 00:07:12.577
to change me.

00:07:12.577 --> 00:07:14.748
Now, no one should try to
change you, but you have

00:07:14.748 --> 00:07:16.331
to change yourself.

00:07:17.287 --> 00:07:20.704
You owe it to everyone to change yourself

00:07:22.426 --> 00:07:25.174
into a better person,
into a better human being.

00:07:25.174 --> 00:07:26.613
That's what you have to do.

00:07:26.613 --> 00:07:31.102
You are perfect, but
you're just not complete.

00:07:31.102 --> 00:07:32.529
So, when you look at yourself,

00:07:32.529 --> 00:07:33.928
look at yourself like that building

00:07:33.928 --> 00:07:36.265
and it's framed up and everything

00:07:36.265 --> 00:07:38.903
is in its right place,
but you just not done.

00:07:38.903 --> 00:07:40.286
I want to tell you that.

00:07:40.286 --> 00:07:41.956
So, anybody who's trying to tell you

00:07:41.956 --> 00:07:44.881
that I'm perfect just the way I am

00:07:44.881 --> 00:07:47.738
is not trying to change and guess what?

00:07:47.738 --> 00:07:49.735
You're not and it's not working.

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:51.603
You're a half done building.

00:07:51.603 --> 00:07:54.141
Who wants to live in a
building with no roof?

00:07:54.141 --> 00:07:57.496
Nobody and I'm just trying
to break it down to you

00:07:57.496 --> 00:07:59.446
that you hear these catchphrases.

00:07:59.446 --> 00:08:01.380
You hear this stuff all the time,

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:03.733
but then everybody just takes it and says,

00:08:03.733 --> 00:08:05.704
oh, yeah, I'm perfect just the way I am.

00:08:05.704 --> 00:08:09.077
And you don't change and
your life doesn't change

00:08:09.077 --> 00:08:11.538
and nothing gets better for you

00:08:11.538 --> 00:08:14.278
and you wonder what's
happening and everything

00:08:14.278 --> 00:08:15.475
is crumbling around you.

00:08:15.475 --> 00:08:17.081
Hey, I'm guilty.

00:08:17.081 --> 00:08:18.812
Terry Crews is guilty, then I realize,

00:08:18.812 --> 00:08:21.165
wait a minute, wait a minute.

00:08:21.165 --> 00:08:23.241
I'm not perfect just the way I am.

00:08:23.241 --> 00:08:25.936
I have to be perfected.

00:08:25.936 --> 00:08:28.826
I am perfect, but I am not complete.

00:08:28.826 --> 00:08:31.973
The thing about self-discipline
is that it is necessary

00:08:31.973 --> 00:08:35.310
for everything you do in your life.

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:38.131
You have to be self-disciplined.

00:08:38.131 --> 00:08:40.105
If discipline comes from somewhere else,

00:08:40.105 --> 00:08:43.879
it's very, very hard to remain consistent

00:08:43.879 --> 00:08:45.184
because you tend to resist.

00:08:45.184 --> 00:08:48.208
It's wild because I see
trainers and they're

00:08:48.208 --> 00:08:51.807
in the gym with people
and, you know, the guy

00:08:51.807 --> 00:08:55.302
or girl that they're working
out hates their workout,

00:08:55.302 --> 00:08:58.205
hates it, because the discipline is coming

00:08:58.205 --> 00:08:59.442
from somewhere else.

00:08:59.442 --> 00:09:02.494
It's something that you
dread every time you go in,

00:09:02.494 --> 00:09:03.934
you don't really want to do it,

00:09:03.934 --> 00:09:07.063
it's like unh, but oh,
no, my trainer's here,

00:09:07.063 --> 00:09:09.867
he's about to beat me up
and make me feel crazy.

00:09:09.867 --> 00:09:14.034
Well, the truth is every
trainer should work his way

00:09:15.332 --> 00:09:16.856
out of your life.

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:19.399
Anybody who's working
you out, your teachers,

00:09:19.399 --> 00:09:22.284
your trainers, your people,
they have to train you

00:09:22.284 --> 00:09:26.435
to get out of your life,
so you can go ahead,

00:09:26.435 --> 00:09:30.126
do your own workout, do your own thing,

00:09:30.126 --> 00:09:31.833
practice self-discipline.

00:09:31.833 --> 00:09:34.959
Now one thing I want to
straighten out big time,

00:09:34.959 --> 00:09:38.209
discipline is not punishment, it's not.

00:09:39.323 --> 00:09:41.240
Discipline is training.

00:09:42.154 --> 00:09:43.350
That's all it is.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.382
I was talking to my son
one time and I asked him,

00:09:45.382 --> 00:09:47.495
it was weird because I
was trying to see if he

00:09:47.495 --> 00:09:49.526
really knew what it was
all about and I said,

00:09:49.526 --> 00:09:51.499
"Hey, man, you know I
have to discipline you.

00:09:51.499 --> 00:09:52.777
"What is discipline?"

00:09:52.777 --> 00:09:56.150
He goes, "Punishment,
punishment, when I do

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.473
"something wrong and you punish me."

00:09:57.473 --> 00:09:59.193
I was like, "No, no."

00:09:59.193 --> 00:10:01.371
Discipline is training.

00:10:01.371 --> 00:10:05.275
If you change your mind,
your mindset and really

00:10:05.275 --> 00:10:08.255
focus it on what discipline really is,

00:10:08.255 --> 00:10:10.941
you start to welcome discipline.

00:10:10.941 --> 00:10:13.359
You welcome self-discipline
into your life.

00:10:13.359 --> 00:10:17.056
If you talk to me and I was into football

00:10:17.056 --> 00:10:19.376
and I was a football player
and you would have told me

00:10:19.376 --> 00:10:21.951
I would be doing what I was
doing, I would have said no,

00:10:21.951 --> 00:10:25.810
you're crazy, leave me
alone, get out of here.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:28.977
This is why life is, you can't predict

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:31.644
what you're supposed to do.

00:10:31.644 --> 00:10:33.472
And I tell people, never
kill yourself, never.

00:10:33.472 --> 00:10:36.280
Because you don't know
what your future is.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.868
You just don't and that's the
thing is, it's like for me,

00:10:39.868 --> 00:10:42.715
I never would have thought
I would be doing this,

00:10:42.715 --> 00:10:44.706
but I decided to try things.

00:10:44.706 --> 00:10:47.653
I just decided that I didn't have to do

00:10:47.653 --> 00:10:50.010
what everyone else said I needed to do.

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:51.815
It's like, you know, when
you're a football player,

00:10:51.815 --> 00:10:54.200
everyone tells you this
would be the best route

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.760
to do after you're done.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:57.549
Well, I decided to go another way.

00:10:57.549 --> 00:10:59.825
And people thought I would fail.

00:10:59.825 --> 00:11:01.758
I remember when I moved
to LA and everybody said

00:11:01.758 --> 00:11:02.896
what are you doing?

00:11:02.896 --> 00:11:04.277
You're an old football player.

00:11:04.277 --> 00:11:05.776
You know what, they don't care.

00:11:05.776 --> 00:11:07.109
And it was hard.

00:11:08.341 --> 00:11:10.309
I was actually doing
security for a little while

00:11:10.309 --> 00:11:14.109
and, you know, we went
broke for a little while,

00:11:14.109 --> 00:11:17.199
but it was an amazing
thing, though, is that

00:11:17.199 --> 00:11:21.588
as I kept trying new things,
new doors kept opening

00:11:21.588 --> 00:11:24.753
and I never thought I would be an actor,

00:11:24.753 --> 00:11:27.561
but here I am, I'm acting.

00:11:27.561 --> 00:11:29.123
I've been acting for 15 years.

00:11:29.123 --> 00:11:31.154
You never know what's going to happen.

00:11:31.154 --> 00:11:34.022
You never know what the
future holds for you

00:11:34.022 --> 00:11:36.882
and it may be acting, it may be business,

00:11:36.882 --> 00:11:41.174
it may be performing,
it may be homemaking,

00:11:41.174 --> 00:11:44.483
but whatever it is,
you have to explore it.

00:11:44.483 --> 00:11:45.680
You have to go for it.

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:47.242
One thing I did is I wrote down my goals.

00:11:47.242 --> 00:11:50.334
I wrote my top ten things
I wanted to do in life

00:11:50.334 --> 00:11:52.890
and if it fit in there, I would do it,

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:55.209
even if it was for free,
even if it was for free

00:11:55.209 --> 00:11:58.078
because the thing is if it fits my goals,

00:11:58.078 --> 00:12:00.435
then it's going to work out somehow.

00:12:00.435 --> 00:12:01.439
- Exactly.

00:12:01.439 --> 00:12:02.440
- You know what I'm saying?

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:03.442
I've done a lot of things for free.

00:12:03.442 --> 00:12:05.433
And they always came and paid me later,

00:12:05.433 --> 00:12:08.359
now if you use money
as the only way to go,

00:12:08.359 --> 00:12:09.961
you going to miss the right thing.

00:12:09.961 --> 00:12:11.746
You going to miss the
right thing you need to do.

00:12:11.746 --> 00:12:15.893
So that's my whole
mentality is just to go out

00:12:15.893 --> 00:12:16.907
all the time.

00:12:16.907 --> 00:12:17.908
I got one speed.

00:12:17.908 --> 00:12:19.628
I'm all in or I'm asleep.

00:12:19.628 --> 00:12:21.443
You know there's no such
thing as overnight success

00:12:21.443 --> 00:12:23.800
because it took a long, long time, I mean,

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:26.621
I've been acting for about
11 years, but to look

00:12:26.621 --> 00:12:30.034
at from when I started to
looking at the billboard

00:12:30.034 --> 00:12:32.618
in Times Square and seeing
The Expendables sitting there,

00:12:32.618 --> 00:12:36.211
that's tremendously fast,
you know what I mean?

00:12:36.211 --> 00:12:39.054
And I've never been in
a hurry because I enjoy

00:12:39.054 --> 00:12:41.066
doing this so much.

00:12:41.066 --> 00:12:44.767
I just enjoy being around
guys like Stallone,

00:12:44.767 --> 00:12:48.523
you know, Mickey Rourke, Randy Coutour,

00:12:48.523 --> 00:12:51.571
just learning how to be a better actor,

00:12:51.571 --> 00:12:52.691
how to be a better person.

00:12:52.691 --> 00:12:55.959
These guys have done major, major things

00:12:55.959 --> 00:12:59.459
in athletics, in life in all kind of ways.

00:13:00.954 --> 00:13:04.353
It kind of took a sports
mentality to my acting

00:13:04.353 --> 00:13:06.385
and that focus.

00:13:06.385 --> 00:13:09.996
It's not about the parties,
it's about the performance,

00:13:09.996 --> 00:13:11.238
you know what I mean?

00:13:11.238 --> 00:13:15.789
My goal was if I was going
to be funny, go all out,

00:13:15.789 --> 00:13:18.169
like go to a point where
they're like wait a minute,

00:13:18.169 --> 00:13:20.807
I can't even air that.

00:13:20.807 --> 00:13:24.485
You got to get rid of
those haters in your mind.

00:13:24.485 --> 00:13:25.722
- Right, it's all in your mind.

00:13:25.722 --> 00:13:29.748
- It's totally it and then
the judgments that you hear

00:13:29.748 --> 00:13:32.392
and you accept, you start
putting that on other people.

00:13:32.392 --> 00:13:33.384
- Totally.

00:13:33.384 --> 00:13:34.396
- So true.

00:13:34.396 --> 00:13:36.229
- When a hater tells you
oh, man, you can't do that,

00:13:36.229 --> 00:13:38.297
that's because he's
hearing that in his head.

00:13:38.297 --> 00:13:39.300
- Yep.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:40.292
- You know what I mean?

00:13:40.292 --> 00:13:41.304
Or you can't lose all that weight.

00:13:41.304 --> 00:13:42.954
That's because he hasn't lost weight.

00:13:42.954 --> 00:13:43.949
- And he doesn't want to.

00:13:43.949 --> 00:13:45.209
He's afraid of the work that it will take

00:13:45.209 --> 00:13:46.712
for him to do it, totally.

00:13:46.712 --> 00:13:50.445
- It's all fear, it's
all, it's a wild, wild mix

00:13:50.445 --> 00:13:52.380
and I just when I'm talking about that,

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:54.311
it's like in your own brain.

00:13:54.311 --> 00:13:56.651
There are times when I
do something so idiotic

00:13:56.651 --> 00:13:59.756
in front of a group of
people just so I can get

00:13:59.756 --> 00:14:01.923
used to getting away from.

00:14:02.827 --> 00:14:03.820
- The norm.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:04.875
- Like fitting in or whatever.

00:14:04.875 --> 00:14:05.875
I do some stupid stuff.

00:14:05.875 --> 00:14:08.394
I'll just say something
dumb, deflect the chicken

00:14:08.394 --> 00:14:11.966
and it's like who cares, who cares.

00:14:11.966 --> 00:14:14.870
If I wear something dumb, who cares?

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.498
If I walk around with a wig on, who cares?

00:14:16.498 --> 00:14:18.106
You can't judge me.

00:14:18.106 --> 00:14:20.599
I have no shame, it's not going to happen.

00:14:20.599 --> 00:14:24.135
And that is where I started
to go like now I can go

00:14:24.135 --> 00:14:25.740
and be free.

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:27.124
- Because there's
nothing holding you back.

00:14:27.124 --> 00:14:28.323
- There's nothing holding me back.

00:14:28.323 --> 00:14:30.070
- What'd you do in high school.

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:33.681
- Listen, I went from
football to basketball

00:14:33.681 --> 00:14:36.756
to track to break dancing,
that's what I did.

00:14:36.756 --> 00:14:40.427
I was, I mean, it was the
middle of the break dance

00:14:40.427 --> 00:14:43.923
phenomenon and I practiced like a fool.

00:14:43.923 --> 00:14:44.925
- Did you have a crew?

00:14:44.925 --> 00:14:47.051
- Oh, yeah, I had a crew, it was all good.

00:14:47.051 --> 00:14:48.681
We were called the Big Man Breakers.

00:14:48.681 --> 00:14:50.324
(laughing)

00:14:50.324 --> 00:14:51.322
Real original.

00:14:51.322 --> 00:14:52.320
- The Big Man Breakers.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.332
- We were real original.

00:14:53.332 --> 00:14:54.329
We were all pretty big.

00:14:54.329 --> 00:14:55.381
- What years was this?

00:14:55.381 --> 00:14:59.080
- Oh, this was 86, 84, I
mean this is at the height.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:00.407
- [Jimmy] Electric Boogaloo.

00:15:00.407 --> 00:15:02.439
- Electric Boogaloo was
out, you know what I mean.

00:15:02.439 --> 00:15:03.453
- [Jimmy] Beat Street.

00:15:03.453 --> 00:15:04.877
- Beat Street, it was hot.

00:15:04.877 --> 00:15:05.910
Yeah, it was hot.

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:06.908
- Really and did you
just throw cardboard down

00:15:06.908 --> 00:15:08.145
and lay it down.

00:15:08.145 --> 00:15:10.402
- We had cardboard in the basement, man,

00:15:10.402 --> 00:15:12.976
and I would practice spinning
on my head for hours.

00:15:12.976 --> 00:15:15.744
I mean, no girlfriends,
nobody would even get near us

00:15:15.744 --> 00:15:17.775
because they're like they're spinning,

00:15:17.775 --> 00:15:19.099
could they stop spinning.

00:15:19.099 --> 00:15:22.118
You know, we want to listen
to some Prince right now.

00:15:22.118 --> 00:15:23.383
Can you please stop spinning.

00:15:23.383 --> 00:15:24.907
- Did you have a go to move?

00:15:24.907 --> 00:15:28.825
- I had the go to move,
which was the robot.

00:15:28.825 --> 00:15:31.658
I have the best robot of all time.

00:15:34.129 --> 00:15:35.475
Play something.

00:15:35.475 --> 00:15:37.975
(funky music)

00:15:45.552 --> 00:15:48.250
(laughing)

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:49.250
- That's how you do it.

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:52.315
(cheering)

00:15:52.315 --> 00:15:53.593
that was a great one.

00:15:53.593 --> 00:15:56.361
- As I get older, the
moves get more subtle,

00:15:56.361 --> 00:15:57.759
because you're like I'm hurting.

00:15:57.759 --> 00:16:00.750
But you see, just a
little, little touches,

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.005
that's all you got to do.

00:16:02.005 --> 00:16:05.016
- You're just so much
energy and so positive.

00:16:05.016 --> 00:16:07.168
How do you stay so positive?

00:16:07.168 --> 00:16:08.842
- You know what, the key to energy,

00:16:08.842 --> 00:16:10.241
I get that asked a lot, they ask me a lot,

00:16:10.241 --> 00:16:13.570
but the key to energy is gratitude.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.280
It's truly, truly gratitude.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.522
(cheering)

00:16:16.522 --> 00:16:17.701
it's real.

00:16:17.701 --> 00:16:21.453
The more thankful you are,
the more energy you get.

00:16:21.453 --> 00:16:23.999
Have you ever, I've been
where I was ungrateful

00:16:23.999 --> 00:16:27.288
and you literally feel the
energy being sapped from you,

00:16:27.288 --> 00:16:28.283
you know what I mean?

00:16:28.283 --> 00:16:30.867
But once you find one
thing to be grateful for,

00:16:30.867 --> 00:16:33.281
all of a sudden you get
the energy to do things.

00:16:33.281 --> 00:16:34.605
I'm from Flint, Michigan.

00:16:34.605 --> 00:16:38.665
I am a statistic that
didn't go by the statistics.

00:16:38.665 --> 00:16:40.961
Because a lot of my friends are in jail,

00:16:40.961 --> 00:16:42.465
a lot of my friends have died.

00:16:42.465 --> 00:16:44.397
A lot of my friends are no longer here

00:16:44.397 --> 00:16:47.213
and I look, here I am, in
front of the whole world,

00:16:47.213 --> 00:16:49.861
all the time, doing what I love,

00:16:49.861 --> 00:16:51.320
which is amazing.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.132
You just feel the energy.

00:16:53.132 --> 00:16:57.227
I feel happy, I feel joy
and that's for you, too.

00:16:57.227 --> 00:16:58.783
Anybody in the world can find that.

00:16:58.783 --> 00:17:01.033
(cheering)

00:17:01.871 --> 00:17:04.371
(funky music)

00:17:09.324 --> 00:17:11.072
- I love this guy, come on.

00:17:11.072 --> 00:17:12.072
Terry Crews.

00:17:15.601 --> 00:17:16.698
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:17:16.698 --> 00:17:19.338
I made this video because
Saketh asked me to,

00:17:19.338 --> 00:17:20.581
so if there's someone
you'd like me to cover

00:17:20.581 --> 00:17:22.774
in the next top ten check out the link in

00:17:22.774 --> 00:17:25.640
the description so you
can go and cast your vote.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:27.673
I also want to give you a quick
shout out to Jane Cassell.

00:17:27.673 --> 00:17:29.805
Jane thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:17:29.805 --> 00:17:32.157
of my book, Your One Word, and
posting that picture online.

00:17:32.157 --> 00:17:34.459
I really appreciate it and I hope

00:17:34.459 --> 00:17:35.842
you're enjoying the read.

00:17:35.842 --> 00:17:37.200
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.442
I believe in you.

00:17:38.442 --> 00:17:40.393
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:17:40.393 --> 00:17:44.025
and whatever your one word is, much love,

00:17:44.025 --> 00:17:45.797
I'll see you soon.

00:17:45.797 --> 00:17:48.130
(swooshing)

00:17:51.662 --> 00:17:54.754
- People have heard
the term purpose a lot.

00:17:54.754 --> 00:17:57.477
They always say, you know,
you've heard the term purpose

00:17:57.477 --> 00:17:59.816
driven life and what's
my purpose and you know,

00:17:59.816 --> 00:18:02.429
I have to be purposeful.

00:18:02.429 --> 00:18:05.346
And the truth is, you know, you do.

00:18:06.378 --> 00:18:08.088
But a lot of people get confused about

00:18:08.088 --> 00:18:10.003
what that really, really means.

00:18:10.003 --> 00:18:12.011
When people think about purpose,

00:18:12.011 --> 00:18:14.429
they think, you know, what's
the purpose of my life.

00:18:14.429 --> 00:18:17.250
My purpose is to be a good person.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:19.895
It's to be a good person.

00:18:19.895 --> 00:18:21.923
And I understand it and you're right.

00:18:21.923 --> 00:18:24.935
You are not wrong about your purpose

00:18:24.935 --> 00:18:26.313
in being a good person.

00:18:26.313 --> 00:18:28.896
But you are not focused enough.

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:31.618
Let me tell you something.

00:18:31.618 --> 00:18:34.872
When I was young, the whole
thing about being purposeful

00:18:34.872 --> 00:18:38.140
or having a purpose, it's
one of those things where

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:42.307
if you don't know exactly
what you do on your job,

00:18:44.746 --> 00:18:46.384
you know, I had a job one time,

00:18:46.384 --> 00:18:48.054
it was really hilarious, I actually worked

00:18:48.054 --> 00:18:51.446
at a liquor store and I was in college

00:18:51.446 --> 00:18:54.824
and I remember just not really knowing

00:18:54.824 --> 00:18:56.263
why I was there.

00:18:56.263 --> 00:18:57.262
(laughing)

00:18:57.262 --> 00:18:59.997
It was just about getting
my money, you know,

00:18:59.997 --> 00:19:02.701
my purpose was to restock some things

00:19:02.701 --> 00:19:04.591
and kind of do some stuff and I remember

00:19:04.591 --> 00:19:07.217
actually applying for another
job in the middle of it

00:19:07.217 --> 00:19:10.486
and I told my boss like, yeah, you know,

00:19:10.486 --> 00:19:12.436
I went for another job,
but I'm just going to

00:19:12.436 --> 00:19:15.222
be here until that other job calls.

00:19:15.222 --> 00:19:17.104
You know she fired me on the spot

00:19:17.104 --> 00:19:19.159
and I was shocked.

00:19:19.159 --> 00:19:20.847
I was like, man, why can't
this woman understand

00:19:20.847 --> 00:19:23.224
that I need some more money.

00:19:23.224 --> 00:19:26.885
But what I didn't
understand was my purpose

00:19:26.885 --> 00:19:28.729
for being there.

00:19:28.729 --> 00:19:31.273
My purpose for being
there was to help her.

00:19:31.273 --> 00:19:34.077
Not be there until I get another job

00:19:34.077 --> 00:19:36.976
and keep my mind all on other things

00:19:36.976 --> 00:19:40.091
because my job was to carry
those big crates of soda,

00:19:40.091 --> 00:19:43.053
to restock the cabinet, restock whatever

00:19:43.053 --> 00:19:45.589
I needed to do and really, you know,

00:19:45.589 --> 00:19:48.218
do the cash register, do
whatever I needed to do,

00:19:48.218 --> 00:19:51.183
but my purpose was messed up, it was whack

00:19:51.183 --> 00:19:52.746
and that's why I got fired.

00:19:52.746 --> 00:19:56.423
Purpose is really about finding out

00:19:56.423 --> 00:19:57.923
what it is you do.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:02.440
What is your role.

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:04.716
A lot of people get this mixed up,

00:20:04.716 --> 00:20:06.053
because let me tell you something.

00:20:06.053 --> 00:20:08.861
You don't get paid for what you know,

00:20:08.861 --> 00:20:11.537
you get paid for what you do.

00:20:11.537 --> 00:20:14.547
That's what you get paid for, that's all.

00:20:14.547 --> 00:20:17.104
People will tell me, oh, I know all that,

00:20:17.104 --> 00:20:19.217
I know this and I know
that, but what you know

00:20:19.217 --> 00:20:21.412
doesn't get you your money.

00:20:21.412 --> 00:20:24.412
Only what you do and to know exactly

00:20:26.735 --> 00:20:29.557
what to do you have to know your purpose.

00:20:29.557 --> 00:20:31.572
If you don't know your purpose,

00:20:31.572 --> 00:20:35.453
you are probably confused
and you'll be out

00:20:35.453 --> 00:20:37.871
and if you don't do what
you're supposed to do,

00:20:37.871 --> 00:20:42.038
the world is going to miss
what you're supposed to bring.

00:20:43.274 --> 00:20:45.855
They're going to miss what you have.

00:20:45.855 --> 00:20:48.195
You must find your purpose.

00:20:48.195 --> 00:20:51.932
You must find what it is
you were always, always

00:20:51.932 --> 00:20:52.926
meant to do.

00:20:52.926 --> 00:20:56.787
That is the biggest fight
ever and once you find it,

00:20:56.787 --> 00:20:59.834
it's the key to your success, it's the key

00:20:59.834 --> 00:21:02.719
to you being who you're supposed to be.

00:21:02.719 --> 00:21:04.792
I am the best over actor ever.

00:21:04.792 --> 00:21:08.227
Like if you give me
something and you tell me

00:21:08.227 --> 00:21:11.313
to do it big, I do it really big,

00:21:11.313 --> 00:21:15.173
but I love that because
it's kind of my personality.

00:21:15.173 --> 00:21:17.916
I'm a very big personality.

00:21:17.916 --> 00:21:20.741
I like doing thing loud,
I like being explosive

00:21:20.741 --> 00:21:24.012
and I like attention, so
it all works together.

00:21:24.012 --> 00:21:25.962
You're going to mess up.

00:21:25.962 --> 00:21:28.844
You're going to see something
that you didn't mean to see,

00:21:28.844 --> 00:21:31.674
you're going to eat something
you didn't mean to eat,

00:21:31.674 --> 00:21:34.397
you're going to overdo
it, you're going to binge,

00:21:34.397 --> 00:21:35.877
you're going to mess up.

00:21:35.877 --> 00:21:38.072
You're going to fail.

00:21:38.072 --> 00:21:39.128
You are.

00:21:39.128 --> 00:21:42.199
Remember what that feels like, remember.

00:21:42.199 --> 00:21:46.178
Because failure really is only temporary

00:21:46.178 --> 00:21:48.147
if you don't take it as a loss.

00:21:48.147 --> 00:21:50.260
If you take is as a learning opportunity,

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:53.414
it's only temporary, but
it can only be permanent

00:21:53.414 --> 00:21:56.073
if you say you lose and you give up.

00:21:56.073 --> 00:21:58.552
That's the only way
things can be permanent.

00:21:58.552 --> 00:22:00.969
Forgive yourself and move on.

00:22:01.839 --> 00:22:03.492
Move on.

00:22:03.492 --> 00:22:06.760
Practice forgetting any of the other junk

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:08.649
that you did, a mistake you did.

00:22:08.649 --> 00:22:09.645
Let me tell you.

00:22:09.645 --> 00:22:12.472
The day is short and let me tell you,

00:22:12.472 --> 00:22:14.963
it's not a thing that you
even have to remember,

00:22:14.963 --> 00:22:19.519
just go on and keep
continuing on the right path.

00:22:19.519 --> 00:22:21.249
When you mess up, start over.

00:22:21.249 --> 00:22:24.988
Start over right away and
I'm trying to tell you

00:22:24.988 --> 00:22:28.337
you do that enough, you
eventually don't mess up.

00:22:28.337 --> 00:22:31.650
You eventually, it's kind of like a child

00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:34.672
who falls down every
time he gets up to walk.

00:22:34.672 --> 00:22:36.460
Well, you know, he will fall down.

00:22:36.460 --> 00:22:37.886
That's just the nature of the beast.

00:22:37.886 --> 00:22:40.144
But let me tell you as time goes on,

00:22:40.144 --> 00:22:44.059
he learns not to fall and you will too.

00:22:44.059 --> 00:22:48.109
You will too, but imagine
if you were a kid,

00:22:48.109 --> 00:22:50.099
if you fell down once
and you just laid there

00:22:50.099 --> 00:22:52.062
and you laid there forever.

00:22:52.062 --> 00:22:54.343
Well, guess what, it doesn't work.

00:22:54.343 --> 00:22:56.944
That is the same way you work.

00:22:56.944 --> 00:22:59.016
That's the same way even adults do.

00:22:59.016 --> 00:23:01.211
Sometimes we fall down, you miss the mark

00:23:01.211 --> 00:23:03.628
and you just stay down there,

00:23:04.561 --> 00:23:06.061
but you can do it.

